## Slack messages

- Always create the message as a draft. Never send it directly — sending is the user's call.
- Audience is developers and tech managers. Keep the tone friendly.
- Shrink every Slack message to short, direct text — no filler.
- Use bold for highlights — the key point, a name, a number worth catching the eye.
- Run the message through the `humanizer` skill (`/humanize`) before drafting, to strip AI-sounding phrasing.